On Wednesday 07 April 2004 07:58 Mark Healey (die@spammer.die) wrote:

> I don't know if "temple" means a room with an altar with priest or
> just a room with an altar.  I currently have a room with an altar and
> staircase.

That's not a temple; it's an altar room. Altars and staircases are both
features that can occur in normal rooms (i.e. not special rooms like
shops and beehives) and they don't get in each other's way.

A temple is a room with an attended altar in the centre: a kind of
special room.

If you convert an altar in a normal room, nothing untoward happens
(except that the god may take issue); if you convert a temple altar the
priest and his god will be pissed off, and if you kill a temple priest
you get ghosts.

